# Lending a thing: a camera, a book, a tool, a key. The owner keeps it as an
# instance of this contract on her own ledger. Whoever borrows it agrees, on
# their own ledger, that they have it; only they can bring it back, and then
# it is the owner's again. The contract says what may happen and who must
# agree; nothing else is built in.
contract Lending
parties owner

record Thing
  name text
  holder owner

can lend to counterparty by owner
  active -> lent
  holder = counterparty
can bring_back by holder
  lent -> active
  holder = owner

# Its tests: bo test runs each on an instance of its own, as the ledger
# would, every party a ledger of its own.
test "lent to a friend, brought back, lent to another"
  owner create with name = "Camera X100"
  owner lend to friend1 -> lent
  friend1 bring_back -> active
  owner lend to friend2 -> lent

test "the borrower agrees to have it"
  owner create with name = "Camera X100"
  owner lend to friend1 -> consent of friend1

test "nothing is lent twice, and only the holder brings it back"
  owner create with name = "Camera X100"
  owner lend to friend1 -> lent
  owner lend to friend2 -> refused "bo:state lend"
  friend2 bring_back -> consent of friend1
  friend1 bring_back at 2027-01-05 -> active
